## Sources of Truth

Read files in full when the task warrants it (see **Doctrine-First**). When reporting back, **never inline their contents wholesale** — pull only what the question needs.

| File | Owns | When you read it |
|---|---|---|
| `reference/recruiting.md` | How the field and recruiting work: funnel, timeline, interview loops, negotiation, four industry tracks. | Strategy, timeline, "how does hiring work," OA prep, track expectations. |
| `reference/resume.md` | The resume document: ATS rules, structure, DRAW/AR bullet doctrine, per-track emphasis. | Formatting, bullets, what to lead with, why an entry is weak. |
| `reference/companies.md` | Company tiers, interview process, OA platform, bottlenecks, notes. | Company specifics, tiering, comparing targets. |
| `context.md` | Candidate state: identity, education, experiences, bullet pool, swap sets, targets. | "Am I competitive," which track, what the candidate actually has; behavioral story sourcing for prep. |
| `network.md` | Referral and contact list. | Who to reach out to, warm intros, follow-ups. |
| `applications/{year}/{company}/company.md` | Per-company intel: funnel, stack, what wins. | Interview prep when a pipeline application exists. |
| `applications/{year}/{company}/{role}/grade.md` | Screen verdict + **Interview angles** (lead with, defend, depth prep). | Primary prep brief when the role was pipelined. |
| `applications/{year}/{company}/{role}/persona.md` | Recruiter lens: bar, track, screen criteria. | What the loop is testing when grade.md is absent or thin. |

`applications/{year}/TRACKER.md` is the empirical application log for calibrating likelihood estimates. Columns: Company, Role, Date Applied, Status, Track, **Score** (`display_score` from `grade.md`, or `—` if not pipelined).

**Division of labor:** `reference/recruiting.md` is general truth (e.g. behavioral is a filter round); `reference/companies.md` is the company-specific instance (e.g. Amazon LPs, a firm's CodeSignal bar).

